# CSF3 remote execution

When running tests, training, data sync, or Slurm jobs for this dissertation:

1. Read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/CSF/ssh-access.md`, and `docs/CSF/csf-environment.md` (always `module load miniforge` + `PATH=$HOME/.local/bin` on CSF).
2. Run cluster commands via **`ssh csf3 '…'`** from the user's Mac (BatchMode when multiplex master is active). If connection fails, ask the user to run `ssh -Y csf3` and approve Duo.
3. **Paths:** code `~/comp30030-mirage-ablation`; large data `~/scratch/comp30030-mirage-ablation` (absolute paths in `runs/registry.yaml`).
4. **No training on CSF login nodes** — use `sbatch` per `docs/workflow_stages/execution_plans/2026-09-10-perception-imagery-latent-ablation-execution-plan.md` § CSF3.
5. Follow `docs/workflow_stages/execution_plans/2026-09-10-perception-imagery-latent-ablation-execution-log.md` blockers and gates before GPU work or Track B ablation reporting.
